  "text": "That sounds like a wonderful idea! A classic breakfast omelette is a simple but delicious way to show your mom how much you care. Here's a basic recipe to make a classic omelette:\n\n### Classic Breakfast Omelette Recipe\n\n#### Ingredients:\n- 2 to 3 large eggs\n- 1/4 cup milk (optional, for fluffiness)\n- 1/2 teaspoon salt\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 teaspoon butter or oil (for cooking)\n- Optional: cheese (cheddar, Swiss, or your mom's favorite), cooked vegetables (like spinach, mushrooms, or bell peppers), or cooked meat (like ham or bacon)\n\n#### Instructions:\n1. **Crack the eggs** into a bowl and whisk them together with the milk, salt, and pepper.\n2. **Heat a non-stick skillet or frying pan** over medium heat and add the butter or oil.\n3. **Pour the egg mixture** into the pan. Let it cook undisturbed for about 1-2 minutes, until the edges start to set.\n4. **Use a spatula** to gently lift the edges of the omelette, allowing the uncooked part to flow underneath.\n5. **When the omelette is just set**, add your desired fillings (cheese, vegetables, meat) to one half of the omelette.\n6. **Fold the other half** over the fillings and let it cook for another 1-2 minutes.\n7. **Slide the omelette** onto a plate and serve warm.\n\n#### Tips:\n- You can add a sprinkle of herbs like parsley or chives for extra flavor.\n- If you're unsure about the timing, you can loosely cover the pan with a lid to help the eggs cook more evenly.\n- For a richer flavor, use whole eggs and don't add milk.\n\nThis classic omelette is not only delicious but also easy to customize based on what your mom likes. It\u2019s a perfect way to spread some love and make her Mother's Day extra special!\n\nLet me know if you'd like a version with a chocolate twist, just for fun! \ud83c\udf6b\ud83c\udf73",
